      "message": "Is the right way to do this to add aliases like conscrypt?\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/conscrypt/common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/OpenSSLProvider.java;drc\u003d04b2b0e206afe64d33baca8bc602f1f13ca0d6d2;l\u003d208\n\n```\nput(\"KeyFactory.XDH\", PREFIX + \"OpenSSLXDHKeyFactory\");\nput(\"Alg.Alias.KeyFactory.1.3.101.110\", \"XDH\");\n```\n\nThough, now that I think about it, we don\u0027t seem to be supporting these aliases for anything else. So it is probably not appropriate to add now. However, do you think we should file a bug? IMO it would be good for Android to be as compatible with other providers as possible.",
