      "side": 0,
      "message": "As far as I can tell, this is how we\u0027re doing it: Mapping a specific key (\"KeyFactory.XDH\") to a class to be instantiated when the user asks the factory for a KeyFactory for that algorithm.\n\nPrashant\u0027s work on porting Wycheproof tests to CTS will uncover where we\u0027re incompatible.\n\nHowever there\u0027s limited compatibility we can provide, because the Android Keystore requires a name for each generated key. AFAICT this pretty much forces the caller to use the (Android-specific) KeyGenParameterSpec.\nMy plan is to support all the factories mentioned by the JEP.\n\nThis CL does it for KeyPairGenerator (where the user would get an exception if they do not use a KeyGenParameterSpec) and KeyFactory (where I think we need more work because we\u0027re missing some Conscrypt classes).  I think support for KeyAgreement can be added later, again depending on Conscrypt changes.",
